[StudySlug "ruy-lopez-white"]
[StudyTitle "The Ruy Lopez"]
[StudySummary "A classical 1.e4 repertoire built on the Closed Ruy Lopez, with answers to the Berlin, the Marshall and the third-move sidelines."]
[StudySide "white"]
[StudyECO "C60-C99"]
[Event "Closed Main Line"]
[Site "ChessOpeningStudies"]
[ECO "C88"]
[Orientation "white"]

{The Ruy Lopez begins by attacking the knight that defends e5. The threat is
slow rather than immediate, and White's real plan is to build a big centre
behind it.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6
{Black almost always asks the question first. Retreating keeps the bishop on
its best diagonal.}
4. Ba4 (4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O {The Exchange Variation is playable but hands Black
the bishop pair.}) 4... Nf6
(4... Nxe4 {The Open Defence. Grab the centre back rather than the pawn.}
5. d4 b5 6. Bb3 d5 7. dxe5 Be6)
5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6
(7... O-O 8. c3 d5 {The Marshall Attack. Black gives a pawn for lasting
initiative, so know this or sidestep it.} 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 c6)
8. c3 O-O 9. h3
{The point of the whole set-up: stop ...Bg4 before playing d4.}
9... Na5
(9... Nb8 {The Breyer, rerouting the knight to d7.} 10. d4 Nbd7)
(9... Bb7 {The Zaitsev.} 10. d4 Re8)
10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7 *

[Event "Berlin Defence"]
[Site "ChessOpeningStudies"]
[ECO "C67"]
[Orientation "white"]

{Against the Berlin we head for the endgame. Black's structure is damaged and
the king has lost the right to castle, which is worth more than the bishop pair
at club level.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O Nxe4
(4... Bc5 5. c3 O-O 6. d4)
(4... d6 5. d4 Bd7 6. Nc3)
5. d4 Nd6 6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. dxe5 Nf5 8. Qxd8+ Kxd8 9. h3 Bd7
(9... Ke8 10. Nc3 h6)
10. Rd1 *

[Event "Third Move Alternatives"]
[Site "ChessOpeningStudies"]
[ECO "C64"]
[Orientation "white"]

{Everything else on move three. None of it is dangerous if you meet it with
the centre.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Bc5
(3... f5 {The Schliemann. Sharp, but the centre opens in White's favour.}
4. Nc3 fxe4 5. Nxe4 d5 6. Nxe5)
(3... d6 {The Steinitz Defence. Solid but passive.} 4. d4 Bd7 5. Nc3 Nf6 6. O-O)
(3... Nge7 4. Nc3 g6 5. d4)
4. c3 Nf6 5. d4 Bb6 6. O-O *
